==Battleground==
*1 [[Techn-Old Hyena]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*2 [[H. Nah]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*2 [[Red EnerG]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Techn-Old Hyena]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*2 [[H. Nah]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Red EnerG]]s spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Techn-Old Hyena]]s spawn after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
At the start, try to kill the first Techn-old Hyena before H. Nah comes in. From there, send out [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] to control the hyena horde while using forms of chip damage like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]], Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]], [[Bullet Train Cat]]. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can wreck havoc here, while [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]]'s Sage Slayer allows her to actually be a strong unit against not only the hyena horde, but Techn-Old in particular.

If you don't want to play the stage normally, you can try cheesing it: first lure the first Techn-Old whilst deploying a couple slimes until he reaches your base, then spawn Bahablast. After Bahamut attacks, spawn [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] & when he attacks again, BTrain. After Techn-Old falls, deploy a [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell]] to intercept H Nah, & then just spam attackers until he dies; use the bounty to deploy Idi:NX. Continue spamming & you win, just make sure that when Red Energ arrives, knock him back with [[Ototo Corps|Breakerblast]] or else your stack will die to his surges.

